---
seoTitle: "About GameNews: How We Cover Game News"
seoDescription: "How GameNews covers upcoming PC games and official publisher news, with dated sources and links to the original announcements."
---

GameNews follows upcoming games and official gaming announcements. Our editorial features help readers decide which games to keep on their radar and which questions to ask before launch.

## Who publishes GameNews

Hamza Hanif publishes GameNews. The site name stays GameNews, and editorial articles keep that byline. The byline is the site’s editorial desk, not a claim that the publisher played the game.

The public email is [hamzahanifadsense@gmail.com](mailto:hamzahanifadsense@gmail.com), listed on the [contact page](/contact).

## How our features are made

Our features are AI-assisted, source-based editorial articles. They link to official publisher material and state when information was checked. They are not hands-on reviews, benchmarks, or promises about final quality. We do not label a game as trending without dated evidence.

## How update headlines work

The Game Updates section checks the official Steam announcement feeds for selected games. Each line shows the game, the publisher’s date, and a link to the official post. GameNews does not copy the announcement into its own page.

The feed checks when you visit, every 15 minutes while the page is open, and when you return to the tab. When a source is unavailable, the last saved headlines stay visible with their original dates. Longer editorial features remain publication-dated snapshots and are updated separately.

## Images and links

Game covers and the GTA VI banner are the publishers’ own promotional images, shown with a credit and a link to the official source. GameNews does not claim a separate reuse license or an endorsement. The GameNews logo and favicon are original marks created for this site. Copyright remains with the respective rights holders.

We do not host game files or app installers. Product links lead to official sources.
